Install to /var/lib/alloy/mysql-secret (owner `alloy`, chmod 600 — holds a DB
password). Read by the `local.file "mysql_secret"` component in
alloy-config.alloy, which feeds it straight into `prometheus.exporter.mysql`
as the connection string.

Format is a go-sql-driver DSN: user:pass@tcp(host:port)/ — note there is NO
trailing newline in the real file. Writing it with a plain `echo` instead of
`printf` (or `echo -n`) adds one, which breaks the exporter with
`Error 1102 (42000): Incorrect database name '\n'` (the driver reads
everything after the last `/` as the database name).

Example (replace with the real `alloy_exporter` password):
alloy_exporter:CHANGE_ME@tcp(127.0.0.1:3306)/
